e simple storylines in the comic  books don't sit well with those that may  have way too many questions about  crystal gems because let's be honest a  lot of those questions are still  unanswered so it looks like we won't get  the answers from comic books Sailor Moon  here's an interesting fact did you know  that Rebecca sugar has a hidden secret  not many people have known but it  actually connects to Steven universe  well it's sort of a hidden secret but  fans of the show have actually compared  Rebecca sugars look to the cute  animation character from Sailor Moon and  know they're not the same person but for  some strange reason Steven universe  still pays homage to Sailor Moon the  show features plenty of popular culture  references and we can even see that  Steven has some Sailor Moon manga in his  room you can also notice several moments  the Steven universe characters do that  are almost identical to the movement of  Sailor moons characters fans of the show  are always looking for new references to  Sailor Moon it's unclear whether Rebecca  sugar is actually just paying homage to  an anime she loves or if there are any  other secret connections between the two  shows we'll definitely be keeping an eye  on this one as we can really see more of  Sailor Moon in Steven universe but we're  still not over just how much the  animation character resembles Rebecca do  you think it's all just a bit of  coincidence or disre baka really have a  doppelganger Novak stories here's  another fact as of March 2018 Steven  universe hasn't really had a lot of  backstories of certain characters  everyone wants to know more about in  fact the entire fifth season never  really focused on amethyst so far we  know that amethyst is out of control and  she loves to be a rebel although she  acts tough she indulges in a lot of  self-loathing and we all know that she  has a troubled past  but the past was never really explained  properly and people have so many  questions everyone wants to know more  about amethyst shape-shifting and why  she ended up the way she did apart from  amethyst we also had never seen Pearl's  backstory either it's not yet clear who  pearl belongs to or why she can never  really talk about her past  since the storyline has a strong fantasy  vibe it allows Rebecca sugar to really  play around with possible new plots but  that only leaves the fans feeling  frustrated since there are so many  Steven universe questions people would  just love to have answers - do you mind  that the show went on for so long but  there are still hardly any backstories  given on these complex characters if you  could ask Rebecca sugar one question  what would it be let us know in the  comments unhealthy relationships one of  the few surprising elements this show  does really well is exploring unhealthy  relationships and teaching teens and  adults to watch the show and how to  resolve them will focus on lapis and  Jasper's relationship which was also  brought up by Rebecca sugar herself she  said that she had never really seen a  cartoon do this but she wanted to  express a story that was very much real  in people's lives and it was important  to address it lapis and Jasper are in a  complicated relationship in which laugh  has spelt like she had no control which  caused her to be angry and she really  was angry and led out all of her anger  on Jasper and Rebecca points out that  she was so angry it didn't even matter  who her anger was aimed at but then her  anger disappeared once they separated  and in a predictable turn of events  Jasper knows exactly what to do to win  her back lapis goes into this  self-destructive state which is often  what the actual victims of unhealthy  relationships do there's also of course  the case of Jasper forcing diffused with  lapis when she  doesn't want to overall this is an  extremely important highlight of an  unhealthy relationship and it's just one  of the things this show does extremely  well Nicki Minaj we bet not even all  Nicki Minaj fans know this fact and it  definitely wasn't promoted enough but  Nicki Minaj did actually appear in  Steven universe this was back in 2014  and although she was only featured for  one episode it definitely should have  been talked about more how and why it  happened no one actually knows but  Rebecca sugar stated she absolutely  loved working with Nicki Nicki appeared  as the character called sugilite which  is an amazing fusion between amethyst  and garnet of course we all know they  would fuse into something totally epic  but did anyone expect Nicki Minaj to  voice that character we definitely  didn't sugilite appeared in two episodes  although she was only speaking in one of  them even though we probably won't ever  see sugilite again since we all know  Nicki's expensive it was just really  cool to see Nicki in such a crazy  cartoon and in a character that has a  larger-than-life personality just like  she does speaking of we'd absolutely  love an animated version of Nicki Minaj  Nikki hasn't addressed the Steven  universe episode just yet but we have a  feeling she definitely enjoyed playing  the independent suji lights the question  is will we see more of suji light or was  that just a one-of-a-kind addition to  this crazy but an amazing show we'll  have to stay tuned to find out and  that's all for our video don't forget to  subscribe to the things and tell us how  you felt about this video thanks for  watching see you next time  [Music]
 

